    "notes": "Clips >= 0.5s are loudness-normalised toward -16 LUFS integrated (ffmpeg ebur128 for measurement, gain + alimiter look-ahead true-peak limiter for the correction); shorter clips are peak-normalised. The one inviolable rule is that no clip may exceed -1 dBFS true peak, and every clip is checked with ebur128 after writing. Sparse, high-crest effects (clicks, camera shutters, typewriter keys, heartbeat, impact/boom tails) physically cannot reach -16 LUFS while staying below -1 dBFS - their crest factor is 20-30 dB, so -16 LUFS would need peaks of +5..+8 dBFS. Those clips are flagged loudness_limited=true and sit quieter; no clip is boosted into clipping to chase the loudness target. Clips < 0.5s report lufs_integrated=null because EBU R128 integrated loudness is undefined that short."
